  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Great Apes Conservation Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this proposal is to conserve Gunung Palung National Park, an important protected area for orangutans and gibbons through a program that uses health care benefits as an incentive for villagers to stop illegal logging. This will be done by: 1) carrying out low-cost reforestation of orangutan corridors; 2) carrying out a Turn Your Debt to Forest campaign that encourages villagers to repay their debt to the ASRI health clinic by providing seedlings (that will be used to reforest orangutan habitat); 3) developing alternative livelihoods for people engaged in illegal logging such as organic farming and fishing; 4) expanding the illegal logging monitoring program; and 5) developing a How-to Manual for replicating the ASRI program in other locations.</narrative>
  </description>
